# Section 6, ORS and SRS (the dialogs re-emitted by hand 2026-10-19 morning, now generated).
# s06_ors_coro: CoroExample.in, the first near-field reference surface (element 5, PropType NF1) set 4%
#   long with MODify; ORS recovers the design 6.3293 (5 figures).
# s06_ors_starved: a COPY of ImageDemo.in with its primary's tenth Zernike coefficient set to 5 mm (the
#   defect the PDF line wrap made, finding 1.2 (cc)); ORS names the starved trace and aborts.
# s06_srs_cass: CassWithExitPupil.in, the detector (element 6) slaved to the exit-pupil Return surface
#   (element 5); the OPD at the detector afterwards is at the round-off floor (a bound, pin rule 1) --
#   the sentence after the dialog says so, the opd 6 below checks it.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CoroExample.in s06
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in s06
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in s06
cd $TMP/s06
old CoroExample.in
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_ors_coro
mod
fElt(5)=6.6
q
ors
5
yes
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
! perl -i -pe 's/-3\.536721061D-05/5d0/' ImageDemo.in
old ImageDemo.in
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_ors_starved
ors
12
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
old CassWithExitPupil.in
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_srs_cass
srs
6
5
yes
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
opd 6
/null
# EXPECT: fElt\(\s*5\) =\s+6\.600000000D\+00\s+KrElt[\s\S]*?Old f=\s+6\.600000000D\+00\s+New f=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: ORS: only\s+\d+ of\s+317 test rays reach element\s+11 \(the surface before it\); at least 3 are needed\.\s+ORS: command aborted\.
# EXPECT: Enter number of element to slave to: \[1\]: 5\s+Reference surface recalculation results:[\s\S]*?1\.500000000D\+00\s+1\.50000\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+\d\.\d+D-1[1-9]
# EXPECT-NOT: TTL OPD=\s+NaN
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
